WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.808
Memory consolidation is the process, described here at a practical high level, by which learning can become more stable and integrated over time.

2
00:00:09.808 --> 00:00:14.499
A new lesson or practice attempt may begin as fragile exposure.

3
00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:19.190
Through review, retrieval, feedback, and time, it can become more durable.

4
00:00:19.190 --> 00:00:23.028
Sleep is one support condition in that broader cycle.

5
00:00:23.028 --> 00:00:29.851
This does not mean a learner can skip practice and expect sleep to do the work.

6
00:00:29.851 --> 00:00:34.116
Consolidation works best when there is something meaningful to consolidate.

7
00:00:34.116 --> 00:00:41.365
Focused study, retrieval practice, examples, and correction create better learning material for the system to work with.

8
00:00:41.365 --> 00:00:47.335
If the initial session was shallow, confused, or unfocused, later recall may remain weak.

9
00:00:47.335 --> 00:00:51.600
All-night cramming can be misleading because it feels productive.

10
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:58.849
The learner spends many hours with the material and may feel fluent while the notes are visible.

11
00:00:58.849 --> 00:01:03.114
But sacrificing sleep can weaken attention, recall, judgment, and transfer.

12
00:01:03.114 --> 00:01:11.643
The next day, the learner may recognize the topic but struggle to retrieve it or use it under real conditions.

13
00:01:11.643 --> 00:01:15.054
Use sleep as part of the learning cycle.

14
00:01:15.054 --> 00:01:17.613
Spread learning across days when possible.

15
00:01:17.613 --> 00:01:21.024
Review before forgetting has done too much damage.

16
00:01:21.024 --> 00:01:23.583
Practice retrieval instead of only rereading.

17
00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:26.142
Revisit key ideas after sleep periods.

18
00:01:26.142 --> 00:01:30.833
The pattern is simple: learn, retrieve, sleep, review, apply, and correct.

19
00:01:30.833 --> 00:01:35.097
That rhythm is usually stronger than one large, exhausted push.
